ng fixes — the point does not change the outcome, because whether or not limb (a) is met, POL-NS-06 already refunds the fee in full with no compensation. The driver's reference to the rider's no-show history is context only: POL-GEN-01 makes prior_no_show_flags (6) a lifetime counter that cannot ground any finding, and the citable field rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below POL-NS-09(d)'s threshold of 3, so no escalation follows; the driver's statement does not move the case. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d): the arrival timestamp matches its nearest GPS fix, the trace has no gaps and full 100% coverage, the chat count matches trip_record.chat_message_count, and the 4.50 SGD fare line reconciles to the net fee produced by the resolution rule, so confidence is not capped. The monetary effect of 4.50 SGD is below the 8.00 SGD execution threshold of POL-GEN-05 and executes automatically."
